          "text": "For your 420 sq. ft. backyard office with a 10-inch wall thickness, your authoritative planning volume is **9.9 m³**. \n\nHere is how your questions break down regarding code, structure, and timeline:\n\n* **Building Code:** Hemp-lime construction is referenced in Appendix BL of the 2024 International Residential Code. However, model-code inclusion is not proof of local adoption or permit approval; every specific project requires local authority and qualified professional review.\n* **Roof Support:** Hempcrete is non-load-bearing infill rather than structural block. It requires a conventional structural frame (commonly timber framing) to carry roof, floor, wind, and seismic loads.\n* **Timeline:** Finishing the entire build in three weeks is very tight. While cast-in-situ forms can often be removed the next day, hemp-lime naturally cures over about 3 to 6 weeks before final plaster can be applied (though pre-cast blocks can speed up initial masonry work). Furthermore, exact pricing, inventory, engineering, and local permitting timelines cannot be confirmed via live systems.\n\nWould you like to explore whether you are leaning toward cast-in-situ or pre-cast blocks for your backyard office frame?",
